      "id": "scope",
      "type": "layout.comment",
      "name": "Original masks and boundary semantics",
      "description": "Original synthetic images/projects by OpenCVDataflowGUI contributors, MIT. No customer or third-party images. Sparse rectangles have known inclusive bounds; both APIs agree on their area/perimeter and filled mask, despite point order/winding and redundant vertical endpoints. The nested 23x19 fixture deliberately shows limits: native run areas 4,48,196 versus ordinary 4,62,196. Run-linked output is a flat list with no hole parents; ordinary Tree reports depths 0,1,2. Do not substitute polygon areas for foreground pixel counts. Clip/offset returns an 80x80 polygon with origin [500,-250] and bounds [530,-220,80,80] in the shifted frame. Run budget guard rejects before native extraction. Count failure deliberately requires 5 but finds 4, emitting a valid failed inspection. Rasters are enabled here for review, off by default in the tool. Native allocation savings do not eliminate runtime snapshots or outputs.",
